    {
      "id": "KQSGUlEqvP1733woiW51B",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2237.596583425818,
      "y": -2440.600606399382,
      "width": 1382.1634521484375,
      "height": 595,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#343a40",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bBBV",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1438727083,
      "version": 2579,
      "versionNonce": 930175467,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785696947006,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "        Transcoding SVC\n        15. Download video from S3\n        16. Probe Video - FFProbe read from headers\n        17. Transcode Plan - 720p -> 720p, 480p. 360p etc\n        18. Decode once into frames (Expensive) -> Raw Frames\n        19. Encode Frames multiple times (GPU/CPU intensive) -> 720, 480, 360\n        20. Select desired bitrate for each encoding\n        21. Segment into 2-6 seconds segments. (MPEG-TS (Transport Stream,))\n        22. Create segments  videos/123/1080/seg1.ts(modern use fragmented mp4 i.e fmp4\n        23. Create Manifests  - 720/playlist.m3u8 and a master manifest for what resolutions are\navail \n        22,23 - Upload to S3\n        24. Update Vid Metadata to READY\n        25. Drop event to kafka that video Ready\n\n        Prod Systems can have transcodeing to diff format on diff workers etc thingies or have video\nduration based transcoding workers",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "qBj_Vpxgt3VmG-SjdbGfk",
      "originalText": "        Transcoding SVC\n        15. Download video from S3\n        16. Probe Video - FFProbe read from headers\n        17. Transcode Plan - 720p -> 720p, 480p. 360p etc\n        18. Decode once into frames (Expensive) -> Raw Frames\n        19. Encode Frames multiple times (GPU/CPU intensive) -> 720, 480, 360\n        20. Select desired bitrate for each encoding\n        21. Segment into 2-6 seconds segments. (MPEG-TS (Transport Stream,))\n        22. Create segments  videos/123/1080/seg1.ts(modern use fragmented mp4 i.e fmp4\n        23. Create Manifests  - 720/playlist.m3u8 and a master manifest for what resolutions are avail \n        22,23 - Upload to S3\n        24. Update Vid Metadata to READY\n        25. Drop event to kafka that video Ready\n\n        Prod Systems can have transcodeing to diff format on diff workers etc thingies or have video duration based transcoding workers",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "hPod_Gu4M7zdkX_h0zr_K",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2330.765266588886,
      "y": -811.9443202409034,
      "width": 1068.8155517578125,
      "height": 105,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#343a40",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bBD",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 805574219,
      "version": 364,
      "versionNonce": 959502443,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785696341779,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Bitrate: Amount of data used/transmitted per second in a audio or video file.\nKbps for audio ,Mbps for video\nFile size ≈ Bitrate × Duration",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Bitrate: Amount of data used/transmitted per second in a audio or video file.\nKbps for audio ,Mbps for video\nFile size ≈ Bitrate × Duration",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "jtIrgmpDI__0rBLo9gTq8",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2314.23060288515,
      "y": -1806.207559275832,
      "width": 1237.823486328125,
      "height": 560,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#343a40",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bBE",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 822329093,
      "version": 927,
      "versionNonce": 1226225509,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785695858032,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Transcoding: Convert video from one encoding to another\nEncoding : Taking raw video and compressing it using some codec.\n\nWHY?\na. Users can upload in many format but\nstreaming requires special formats which \nare optimal/faster to stream\nb. We need different encodings for video for \nseamless transfer over network for differnt speed connections\nc. Browsers and devices require special format type\n\n\nNote: Video uploaded from phone etc is already encoded. But what is meant by encoding is\nthat this video uploaded is converted to the raw video then converted to\nsome other encoding.\n",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Transcoding: Convert video from one encoding to another\nEncoding : Taking raw video and compressing it using some codec.\n\nWHY?\na. Users can upload in many format but\nstreaming requires special formats which \nare optimal/faster to stream\nb. We need different encodings for video for \nseamless transfer over network for differnt speed connections\nc. Browsers and devices require special format type\n\n\nNote: Video uploaded from phone etc is already encoded. But what is meant by encoding is\nthat this video uploaded is converted to the raw video then converted to\nsome other encoding.\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Fx19RTLdQGDVJGYBQ1qqI",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2341.480445209264,
      "y": -2722.098576396154,
      "width": 1265.0394287109375,
      "height": 175,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#343a40",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bBF",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 271604651,
      "version": 368,
      "versionNonce": 1314328005,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785695868369,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Resolution : Resolution is how many pixels each frame contains. 1080x720\n2. Frame : Just an image. FPS\n3. Codec: Algo used for compress and decompress the video. \n4. Container: A container is the file format or \"wrapper\" \nthat holds your video, audio, and subtitle tracks together in one file. e.g. mp4, mkv, av1, mov",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Resolution : Resolution is how many pixels each frame contains. 1080x720\n2. Frame : Just an image. FPS\n3. Codec: Algo used for compress and decompress the video. \n4. Container: A container is the file format or \"wrapper\" \nthat holds your video, audio, and subtitle tracks together in one file. e.g. mp4, mkv, av1, mov",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "LVVcrelnhHRnI9iMXcQJB",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2349.5915434047597,
      "y": -2926.5191703311416,
      "width": 444.3326190533035,
      "height": 169.851971652668,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#343a40",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bBH",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1073735173,
      "version": 782,
      "versionNonce": 1728083749,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785695866536,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "| Codec           | Usage                            \n| ------------      | ---------------------------       \n| H.264           | Most common                  \n| H.265 (HEVC)  | Better compression           \n| VP9             | Used by YouTube              \n| AV1              | Newest, highest compression \n",
      "fontSize": 19.41165390316205,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "| Codec           | Usage                            \n| ------------      | ---------------------------       \n| H.264           | Most common                  \n| H.265 (HEVC)  | Better compression           \n| VP9             | Used by YouTube              \n| AV1              | Newest, highest compression \n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
